From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:40:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 108/342] meson_hdmi: modes at any pixel clock the HDMI PLL can
 make

The driver offered seven CEA modes and only switched the PLL's OD2
between 74.25 and 148.5 MHz. It now solves for M, the fraction and
OD1/OD2 (VCO 48 MHz * (M + frac/4096), M 53 to 123, the highest VCO the
dividers allow, which is U-Boot's 5940 MHz for its two clocks) and
restarts the PLL when M or the fraction change; only the dividers
changing, it keeps running as before.

The mode list (now up to 32) has the CEA modes the EDID lists by video
code or detailed timing (480p, 576p and VGA added), the VESA DMT modes
of its established and standard timings, and its other detailed
timings, 25 to 297 MHz, up to 1920x1200, progressive only, sorted by
size and refresh. Preferred stays 1080p60, else the boot mode's size,
else the EDID's first detailed timing.

The VPU's sync polarity bits (VPU_HDMI_SETTING 2 and 3, which U-Boot
sets for its positive syncs) now follow the mode, for the VESA modes'
negative ones. SET_DISPLAY_MODE also takes a complete timing that is
not in the list, if the hardware can make it. The frame buffer is
sized for 1920x1200.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
